---
import { LLM_CHAIN } from '../../data/pipeline';
---

<section class="section" id="llm" aria-labelledby="llm-h">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-num">10 · The LLM experiment</p>
        <h2 id="llm-h">Can a local language model forecast demand?</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-sub" data-reveal>
        This study does <strong>not</strong> claim an LLM is inherently a time-series model. It tests a narrower, practical question — with the same disciplined evaluation as every other rung.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="llm-question" data-reveal>
      <p class="mono llm-question__label">The working question</p>
      <p class="llm-question__text">
        Can a general-purpose, locally hosted language model be used as a practical demand forecasting mechanism when provided with structured historical demand information?
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="chain chain--llm" data-reveal>
      {LLM_CHAIN.map((s, i) => (
        <li class="chain__step">
          <span class="mono chain__num llm">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <div class="chain__body">
            <span class="mono chain__label">{s.label}</span>
            <span class="chain__detail">{s.detail}</span>
          </div>
          {i < LLM_CHAIN.length - 1 && <span class="chain__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <div class="llm-notes" data-reveal>
      <div class="llm-note">
        <p class="mono llm-note__label">Output must be structured</p>
        <p class="llm-note__text">
          The model returns a numerical forecast — not prose. The pipeline validates shape, numeric values, ordering, and time alignment. Invalid outputs are logged, never silently repaired.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="llm-note">
        <p class="mono llm-note__label">No future demand in prompts</p>
        <p class="llm-note__text">
          The prompt discloses only the past. Anything else would leak the test period into the forecast — a hard experimental violation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="llm-note">
        <p class="mono llm-note__label">Distinct from foundation models</p>
        <p class="llm-note__text">
          Time-series foundation-model research (Chronos, Time-LLM, Timer, TimeGPT) is literature context for this project — not the core experiment, which uses a local general-purpose LLM via Ollama.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .llm-question {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-1);
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-8);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--c-llm);
  }
  .llm-question__label { color: var(--c-llm); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); }
  .llm-question__text {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.8vw, 2.1rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    font-weight: 500;
    max-width: 34ch;
  }

  .chain__num.llm { color: var(--c-llm); }
  .chain__step { border-top: 2px solid transparent; }
  .chain--llm .chain__step { border-top-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--c-llm) 35%, var(--line)); }

  .llm-notes {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--grid-gap);
    margin-top: var(--sp-7);
  }
  @media (min-width: 56rem) { .llm-notes { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .llm-note {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    background: var(--surface-2);
    padding: var(--sp-5);
  }
  .llm-note__label { color: var(--c-llm); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .llm-note__text { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: var(--fs-body-sm); }
</style>